.TH sane-sp1130n 5 "25 October 2026" "@PACKAGEVERSION@" "SANE Scanner Access Now Easy"
.SH NAME
sane-sp1130n \- experimental Ricoh SP-1130N USB and native LAN backend
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sp1130n
backend is an experimental, hardware-unvalidated scanner driver.
Duplex scanning is the default. Front-only and back-only sources are available.
Do not interpret synthetic test results as successful scans on real hardware.
.PP
Build it explicitly with
.BR "BACKENDS=sp1130n" .
The default backend selection excludes it and the default dll.conf entry is
commented out. To use it, add sp1130n to the process's isolated dll.conf or a
separately reviewed SANE configuration. No vendor library or firmware is loaded.
.SH DEVICES
The USB device ID is 05ca:031e. Device names are
.BR sp1130n:usb:BUS:ADDRESS .
Use the name returned by scanimage \-L. The older non-N SP1130 and other Ricoh
devices are not inferred compatible.
.PP
Native LAN is selected explicitly as
.BR sp1130n:tcp:IPv4
or
.BR sp1130n:tcp:IPv4:PORT .
The default TCP port is 16888. Only numeric unicast IPv4 is accepted.
LAN is not enumerated, and no DNS lookup, broadcast, address change, eSCL or
WSD discovery is performed. Reported encryption is conservatively refused.
Plaintext transfer has no confidentiality or server authentication. Use a
trusted network and non-sensitive, replaceable originals for initial tests.
.SH OPTIONS
The source is ADF Duplex, ADF Front or ADF Back. Modes are Color, Gray or
Lineart. USB resolutions are 300 or 600 dpi; LAN is restricted to full A4 at
300 dpi with front/back output selected on the host. Duplex buffers both sides after one
sheet acquisition and returns the front image followed by the back image.
A client must use start/read/EOF/start/read/EOF without cancelling between sides.
.PP
Physical page dimensions and the tl-x, tl-y, br-x and br-y acquisition window
use integer millimeters on USB. These options are inactive for LAN.
Invalid or unsupported profiles are rejected before scanner I/O.
Brightness, contrast, threshold and back-rotate are computer-side processing.
Autocrop, deskew and skip-blank are optional and disabled by default. Blank
filtering may discard faint marks and changes front/back numbering. At most
32 fully blank sheets are acquired per start.
.PP
LAN retains the image socket and client lock across sheets in one feeder job.
There is no prepare/start/stop cycle between sheets. Cancel requests termination
using lock-free atomic state; bounded cleanup occurs in the next normal backend
call or on close, never in a signal handler. USB finishes pending command/data
transactions and final completion records before cleanup. Its image phase has
a 120-second timeout budget, followed by up to 25 seconds for STOP/unlock.
After end-of-feeder or
a failed LAN job,
cancel or reopen before starting another job. Option changes during a live
job are refused.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SP1130N_EXPERIMENTAL
Must be exactly 1 before scanning. Otherwise sane_start returns unsupported.
Opening a LAN handle is lazy and does not contact the scanner.
.SH EXAMPLE
Replace the example address with the scanner's actual IPv4 address:
.PP
.nf
SP1130N_EXPERIMENTAL=1 scanimage \\
  \-d sp1130n:tcp:192.168.1.50 \-\-source "ADF Duplex" \\
  \-\-batch=side-%03d.pnm \-\-batch-count=2 \-\-format=pnm
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
This initial port is Linux-only and requires libusb-1.0, libjpeg and pthreads.
Only one SANE handle can be open. Discovery, encryption negotiation, scanner
configuration, vendor calibration, maintenance resets and firmware upload are
not implemented. Scanner faults or transport failure can leave a device lock
despite bounded cleanup. A frontend that cancels between pages loses the
buffered back image and ends the feeder job. LAN front/back byte interpretation
is provisional. LAN lock/status and abort cleanup
remain unverified. No physical USB or LAN scanner was tested.
Short-header-only streams without a full side-identifying status record are
unsupported; front/back identity is never inferred from arrival order.
